  "version": "0.6.0",
  "notes": "Nyu is a notebook now, has a menu of her own, and on a Mac UwUNotes feels like a real Mac app ✧\n\n- **New logo:** Nyu is a pink spiral notebook with a pencil behind her ear, in the icon and everywhere in the app\n- **Nyu menu and Nyu-Zentrale:** level, achievements (secret ones show as \"???\" until found), wardrobe, Pomodoro, secrets and Nyu's switches on one page\n- **Updates in Settings:** see your version, check for updates any time and install them right there\n- **Browse the note trash:** its own sidebar view with search, preview, restore, delete for good and empty (also under Datei → Papierkorb anzeigen)\n- **Hide and show the sidebar** with a button right in it; folded, a slim rail with the views stays\n- **Menus fit the window:** long lists scroll, submenus move up or left, nothing scrolls sideways any more\n- **Fonts like UwUMail:** UwU Sans is the new interface font, or Rubik, DM Sans or the system font. The editor can use any installed font, with search\n- **macOS:** the system title bar with traffic lights, every menu in the menu bar with ⌘ shortcuts, Mac-style shortcuts everywhere, quitting from the Dock saves first, an icon in Apple's format, \"Open With\" for text files\n- **Ready for the Mac App Store** (a separate sandboxed build, not submitted yet)\n- C++ and C# can be picked as languages again",
